 # Pennsylvania Broadband Grant

## LHTC Broadband - Expanding Rural Connectivity

LHTC Broadband is actively participating in broadband expansion efforts funded through state and federal grants, including BEAD-related programs, to extend fiber services to unserved and underserved communities in Western Pennsylvania.

### Our Commitment

We are committed to bringing high-speed fiber internet to residents and businesses in Westmoreland, Somerset, and Fayette Counties who currently lack access to adequate broadband services.

### Grant Participation

LHTC Broadband has been designated as a participant in the Pennsylvania Broadband Development Authority's planning process. As BEAD funding becomes available, LHTC Broadband intends to apply for subgrant funding to expand our fiber network into additional unserved areas.

### Current Progress

- Middle mile fiber backbone already in place across much of Western PA
- FTTH expansion underway in select communities
- Permit applications and ROW agreements in progress for new construction zones
- Planning and engineering resources being scaled to meet deployment requirements

---

*For more information, contact us at (724) 593-2411*

